---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="I-Beam Optimization" description="Stress analysis and Python optimization of an asymmetric wooden I-beam." currentPage="/projects">
  <section style="padding:calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-12)) 0 var(--space-8);">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/#projects" style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:var(--text-xs); color:var(--text-tertiary); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em;">← Back to projects</a>
      <span class="section-label" style="margin-top:var(--space-6);">Course Project · ENES220</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:var(--space-2);">Wooden I-Beam Design &amp; Optimization</h1>
      <p style="font-size:var(--text-lg); color:var(--text-secondary); max-width:640px; margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        Derived failure-load equations and built a Python optimizer to balance three
        failure modes for an asymmetric pine I-beam.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card card--featured reveal" data-reveal style="margin-bottom:var(--space-10);">
        <p style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2);"><strong>Course:</strong> ENES220 — Mechanics of Materials</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2);"><strong>Team:</strong> 6 members</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>My role:</strong> Derived the governing equations and wrote the optimization code</p>
      </div>

      <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="I-beam design render" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-md); margin-bottom:var(--space-8); max-height:400px; object-fit:cover; border:1px solid var(--border);" />

      <div class="reveal" data-reveal>
        <h2>Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Design an I-beam cross-section from pine lumber and wood glue that maximizes
          load-carrying capacity. The beam can fail through three mechanisms: flexural failure,
          wood shear failure, and glue-joint shear failure.
        </p>

        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>
          I derived the stress and failure-load equations for all three failure modes from
          first principles. The key insight: the optimal beam should have all three failure
          loads as close to each other as possible.
        </p>
        <p>
          I wrote a <strong>Python optimizer</strong> that parameterized the cross-section
          dimensions and searched for a geometry where the three failure loads balanced
          within 20% of each other. The team then built the beam and tested it to failure.
        </p>

        <h2>Tools</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--space-2); margin-top:var(--space-3);">
          <span class="chip">Python</span>
          <span class="chip">Mechanics of Materials</span>
          <span class="chip">Structural Analysis</span>
          <span class="chip">Lab Testing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:var(--space-12);">
        <a href="/#projects" class="btn btn--outline">← All Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
